f:["$","p",null,{"children":["A ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"store_type: \"cas\""}]," can compress its own uploads and\nfull-blob downloads to the upstream with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_remote_cache_compression"}],".\nBlobs of 64 KiB and above go as ",["$","code",null,{"children":"compressed-blobs/zstd"}],"; smaller blobs and\nranged reads stay on the identity path. The upstream instance must have\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"remote_cache_compression"}]," on its capabilities service, or compressed\nrequests fail with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"InvalidArgument"}],"."]}]
10:["$","p",null,{"children":["Enabling zstd on any capabilities instance or any CAS ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store expresses\nprocess-wide intent. At config load, Forge then turns it on for every\nother CAS ",["$","code",null,{"children":"grpc"}]," store whose ",["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_remote_cache_compression"}]," is\nomitted, so worker-to-CAS and proxy-to-upstream transfers pick it up without\nthe setting being repeated on each store. Declare the intent once and leave\nthe rest inherited:"]}]
